From 467a835b73b1215fb7980fe0ba0b7b9151d90c90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Clinton <stephen_l43@hotmail.co.nz>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:33:14 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(rac1/pal): bootable executable and in-place disc
 image tools

Add two tools for running the build:

- tools/boot_elf.py writes build-sn/SCES_509.16, a bootable executable,
  by laying the linked image's allocated PROGBITS sections over retail's
  container. build-sn/rac1.elf alone is not bootable: its entry point is
  the first .text symbol rather than crt0's _start, it has two PT_LOAD
  segments, and the VU0 microcode at the front of retail's image is not
  linked. The output differs from retail only inside the decompiled
  near-misses, which the tool prints (40 bytes on a clean tree).
- tools/iso_patch.py writes build-sn/SCES_509.16.iso: the owner's image
  with that executable (and optionally the sectors of an
  `editor/extract.py pack` patches.tsv) written in place. The PAL disc
  addresses everything by absolute sector, so same-size replacement is a
  complete repack; a larger executable is refused.

Verified: both the executable (pcsx2-qt -elf) and the image boot in
PCSX2 to the title screen and attract intro, and the image's executable
sectors differ from retail by the same 40 bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
